 "discussions": [
  {
   "id": "d_m6",
   "title": "Discussion: Court Packing: Reform or Power Grab?",
   "html": "<div id=\"sparkled-assessment\"><div style=\"background:#2A2438; border-bottom:4px solid #5B3E96; border-radius:10px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:20px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px; color:#F3C969; margin-bottom:6px;\"><strong>DISCUSSION</strong></div><div style=\"font-family:'Libre Baskerville',Baskerville,Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:26px; color:#FFFFFF; line-height:1.25; margin-bottom:6px;\">Discussion: Court Packing: Reform or Power Grab?</div><div style=\"font-size:15px; color:#ECE6F6;\">10 points · threaded discussion</div></div><div style=\"border-top:3px double #5B3E96; margin:0 0 20px;\"></div><div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD4C4; border-top:4px solid #9B2335; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:18px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#9B2335; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>Before you start</strong></div><p style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 10px;\">Open the lessons \"Social Security and the Wagner Act\" and \"The Court Fight and the Federal Balance\". Use My Notebook on those pages to gather your notes and marks, then come back here to post.</p></div><div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD4C4; border-top:4px solid #2A2438; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:18px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#2A2438; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>The question</strong></div><p style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 10px;\">In 1937, President Roosevelt asked Congress to let him add new justices to the Supreme Court. He said the courts were overworked and the older judges were slow. His critics said he was trying to change the outcome of cases by changing the judges. Was his plan a fair reform, or a grab for power? Your job is to decide which description fits the evidence better.</p></div><div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD4C4; border-top:4px solid #5B3E96; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:18px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#5B3E96; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>Your post</strong></div><p style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 10px;\"><strong>Your post (about 100 to 150 words):</strong></p><ol style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 6px; padding-left:22px;\"><li style=\"margin-bottom:6px;\">Take a clear position: reform, power grab, or a mix that leans one way.</li><li style=\"margin-bottom:6px;\">Give one specific piece of evidence from the lesson \"Social Security and the Wagner Act\" or the source Schechter Poultry Corp. v. United States that supports you.</li><li style=\"margin-bottom:6px;\">Name one fact that cuts against your position, and explain why you still hold it.</li></ol></div><div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD4C4; border-top:4px solid #9B2335; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:18px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#9B2335; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>Your reply</strong></div><p style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 10px;\"><strong>Your reply (about 50 to 75 words):</strong> Respond to one classmate. Do you agree with their reasoning? If so, strengthen it with something they did not use. If not, say respectfully where their reasoning falls short.</p></div><div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD4C4; border-top:4px solid #2A2438; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:18px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#2A2438; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>Before you post</strong></div><p style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 10px;\">Post first, then reply. You will not see your classmates' posts until you have posted.</p></div><div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD4C4; border-top:4px solid #2A2438; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:18px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#2A2438; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>Rubric</strong></div><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; margin-top:6px;\"><tbody><tr><th style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; text-align:left; vertical-align:top; background:#ECE6F6; font-size:14px; width:22%;\">Post and reply<br><span style=\"color:#5B3E96;\">10.0 pts</span></th><td style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; vertical-align:top; font-size:14px;\"><strong>10.0 pts</strong> Substantive<br><span style=\"color:#55524C;\">Clear position, specific evidence from the week, names a counterpoint, and the reply engages a classmate's actual reasoning</span></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; vertical-align:top; font-size:14px;\"><strong>6.0 pts</strong> Thin<br><span style=\"color:#55524C;\">Position stated but evidence vague, no counterpoint, or the reply only says \"I agree\"</span></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; vertical-align:top; font-size:14px;\"><strong>0.0 pts</strong> Missing<br><span style=\"color:#55524C;\">No post, or no reply</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>",
